From 84cad581d42a75bd283d380a87ccc464cb22520b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:50:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 30/32] ARM: dts: broadcom: us-48-500w: Add a ramoops region

1 MiB of DDR in the high bank for pstore (ramoops): the boot health
record (boot counter, clean-shutdown flag) is written to pmsg and read
back at the next boot, so no flash is written.

The region is above the 64 MiB a2 carveout and 10 MiB below the low
end of what awto-uboot reserves at the top of DDR (relocated image,
malloc pool, stack, FDT: 0x6eaff520..0x6fffffff). At 0x6fc00000 the
region sat inside that malloc pool and was zeroed on every reboot. The
health line reports rec=ram/prev=none when the record does not survive.

Signed-off-by: TODO
---
 .../dts/broadcom/bcm53344-ubnt-unifi-us-48-500w.dts    | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm53344-ubnt-unifi-us-48-500w.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm53344-ubnt-unifi-us-48-500w.dts
index b893735bd..0867ce388 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm53344-ubnt-unifi-us-48-500w.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm53344-ubnt-unifi-us-48-500w.dts
@@ -47,6 +47,16 @@ a2_mem: a2@4000000 {
 			reg = <0x04000000 0x04000000>;
 			reusable;
 		};
+
+		/* us48-health boot record (pstore pmsg, RAM only): above the a2 carveout, below awto-uboot's malloc + stack */
+		ramoops@6e000000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0x6e000000 0x100000>;
+			no-map;
+			record-size = <0x10000>;
+			console-size = <0x40000>;
+			pmsg-size = <0x40000>;
+		};
 	};
 
 	/* Consumer of a2_mem and carrier of the layout inside it */
